{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>What shall we say to my lord.</b> To respond to your words when you said <b>what is this deed</b> — for indeed?" "<b>How shall we speak.</b> To deny that we did this, even though the judgment is against us?" "<b>And how shall we justify ourselves.</b> To demonstrate in straightforwardness that the entire affair was a contrivance to take advantage of us?" "<b>Elohim has found the iniquity of your servants.</b> It is not for this that we are being punished — for we did not sin in this at all. Rather, because of an iniquity we committed long ago, the El wished to punish us, to exact retribution from us through you — after the manner of מֵרְשָׁעִים יֵצֵא רֶשַׁע (1 Samuel 24:14) — as stated by Lulianus and Pappus (Eikhah Rabbati), who said: 'We have incurred much liability for death before HaShem; but there are many agents of HaShem — bears and lions — that attack us, yet He exacts from us only through you, who are destined to demand our blood from your hand.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {3 "Sforno reads להתעולל as 'to deal harshly with / take advantage of us.' The citation from Lulianus and Pappus is drawn from Eikhah Rabbati 1:16; the phrase הרבה שלוחים למקום is rendered 'many agents of HaShem,' understanding למקום as למקום (to HaShem, i.e., divine agents)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:35.164897053Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}